{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 5339,
    "dDurationMs": 1091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "TOP 10 REASONS Why We Know the Earth is Round\n10."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6430,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the other planets and stars we've ever\nseen are round and there's no reason to indicate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10269,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the earth should be any different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11929,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "9."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12929,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Time Zones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13929,
    "dDurationMs": 3491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Day and night happen at different times at\ndifferent places on earth - in fact, it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17420,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "always day somewhere and night somewhere else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20180,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21180,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Coriolis Effect means freely moving things\n(like cannonballs or hurricane winds) are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25010,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deflected to the right - but only if you're\nnorth of the equator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28000,
    "dDurationMs": 2789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're south of the equator, they're deflected\nleft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30789,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "7."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31789,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Triangles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32789,
    "dDurationMs": 5421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you walk 10,000km straight along the earth's\nsurface, turn 90° to your right, walk 10,000km"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38210,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more, turn right again and walk another 10,000km,\nyou will be back to where you started, having"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42700,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "successfully made a triangle with three 90°\nangles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45450,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As any geometry student can tell you, this\nis impossible on a flat surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49690,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "6."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50690,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sun, in general, gets lower and lower\nin the sky as you travel away from the equator"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54489,
    "dDurationMs": 2741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can use this to measure the earth's\ncurvature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57230,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pick two places a few hundred miles directly\nnorth and south of each other and at noon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60890,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measure the shadows cast by a vertical meter-stick\nat each location."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64100,
    "dDurationMs": 3159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can use the shadow-lengths to figure out\nthe angle between the sticks and once you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67259,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "add in how far apart they are, you can calculate\nthe earth's curvature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70529,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "5."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71529,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The stars at night change as you go north\nor south - for example, Orion is upside down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75979,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you're in Australia!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77639,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78639,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ferdinand Magellan (and many people afterwards)\ncircumnavigated the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82149,
    "dDurationMs": 4091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means he left headed west, continued\ngoing west, and came back to where they started,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86240,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still going west (actually, Magellan was dead,\nbut one of his ships - led by Juan Sebastián"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90289,
    "dDurationMs": 1661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Elcano - finished the journey)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91950,
    "dDurationMs": 3399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you head west and circumnavigate the earth\nyourself, you'll be able to tell because you'll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95349,
    "dDurationMs": 2821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "observe one fewer sunrise than everyone who\nstays at home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98170,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "3."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99170,
    "dDurationMs": 1269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The horizon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100439,
    "dDurationMs": 3911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ships on the ocean or tall Chicago buildings\nviewed over Lake Michigan disappear bottom-first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104350,
    "dDurationMs": 4589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can see the sun set twice if you watch\nit lying down and then quickly stand up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108939,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The simple fact is, if the earth were flat,\nthere wouldn't be a horizon beyond which things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113189,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could disappear so you'd be able to see all\nof Chicago from across Lake Michigan…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117299,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as the rocky mountains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118899,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119899,
    "dDurationMs": 3481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During a lunar eclipse, the shadow of the\nearth on the moon is curved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123380,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124380,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125380,
    "dDurationMs": 34590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We know the earth is round because we have\nphotographic evidence."
    } ]
  } ]
}
